Data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Material and contact values in library/ (materials, pairs, objects) are facts taken from the handbooks, standards,
data sheets and papers cited in each card's note and in library/SOURCES.md, or our own estimates, marked as such
(source: model). Meshes in library/meshes are generated by alloy/cards/meshgen.py from those dimensions.

The object library on the Hugging Face Hub (argonrobotics-ai/alloy-library) is not part of this distribution; its
ATTRIBUTION.md credits each source. Its 1,900 kitchen objects and fixtures were made by Lightwheel (NVIDIA's
PhysicalAI-Robotics-Manipulation-Objects-Kitchen-MJCF dataset, CC BY 4.0, as packaged by RoboCasa), with our
collision hulls, estimated masses and materials.

The scan-texture test fixture in tests/camera/data/scan_fixture is cut down from the 004_sugar_box scan of the YCB
Object and Model Set (B. Calli, A. Walsman, A. Singh, S. Srinivasa, P. Abbeel, A. M. Dollar; ycbbenchmarks.com), CC BY
4.0; the ATTRIBUTION.md beside it lists the source and our changes.

The reference-task data (task scenes and their card values, materials, pairs and meshes, the yam_bench robot's
scene, the T12 task pack in bench/xbench/ours/packs/t12) is Copyright Argon Robotics, licensed under Apache-2.0 like
the rest of Alloy; the YAM robot meshes in it are I2RT's (above).
